# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_schema_precision.py" "SCHEMA PRECISION GATE: PASS" "schema-coupling precision: ubiquitous table-name false-coupling is recall-safely demoted by the engine, NOT dropped at extraction" "schema-coupling precision RECALL GUARD: the ubiquitous-table-NAME false coupling (two unrelated files both touching \`users\`/\`tags\`/\`id\`) is REAL in the raw graph (measured on saleor/django-oscar/discourse: discourse \`users\` couples 1054 pairs whose co-change 1.3% tracks RANDOM 0.3%, while SPECIFIC-name pairs co-change ELEVATED 7.6%). BUT the recall-safe fix ALREADY lives in the engine: every ubiquitous-named table in all 3 repos is a RESOURCE HUB (saleor user=39, discourse users=191/tags=33 touchers, all > hub threshold), so the engine's res-hub dampening suppresses EVERY ubiquitous-only schema pair (0 survive after dampening) while specific pairs stay elevated (14-33%). A name-based ubiquitous-schema-name STOPLIST at EXTRACTION is therefore REDUNDANT and RECALL-RISKY: a SMALL repo whose real central table is generically named (\`record\`/\`status\`, only 2-3 touchers, NOT a hub) would be SILENTLY DROPPED by a name stoplist, whereas hub dampening keeps it (few < hub) AND demotes the genuine hub. CARDINAL RULE: when in doubt KEEP; never DROP a specific table coupling. This gate PINS that boundary on a hermetic synthetic graph: the extractor KEEPS the ubiquitous-hub edges raw (a future 'precision fix' that drops them at extraction FAILS here = recall loss), the engine's hub dampening demotes the ubiquitous hub out of confident coupling, and a specific low-participant table + a GENERIC-named low-participant real table (the stoplist-unsafe case) + the migration<->code moat catch are ALL kept (recall). Content-free (table NAMES + edge kinds only); no DB, no network" "schema-coupling precision: ubiquitous-table-name over-coupling is recall-safely demoted by the engine's resource-hub dampening (not by a recall-risky extractor stoplist); specific + generic-named-low-participant + migration<->code couplings all kept; conclusion PINNED against a future extractor stoplist" 12
